# Project TODOs

Welcome to your newly scaffolded `{{.AppName}}` project! Here are the next steps to get your project fully production-ready based on the features you selected.

{{- if .Features.API}}
## API & Authentication
- [ ] **Authentication**: The boilerplate provides middleware placeholders in `internal/auth/auth.go`. `BearerTokenMiddleware` rejects every request until you pass it a `TokenValidator` implementing your auth scheme (e.g., JWT validation, OAuth 2.0 + PKCE, or OIDC).
- [ ] **OpenAPI Spec**: Update `openapi.yaml` to match any new endpoints you add, or consider generating it automatically from code comments using tools like `swag`.
{{- end}}

{{- if .Features.UI}}
## UI (Frontend)
- [ ] **Branding & Theme**: Customize the Tailwind CSS theme in `web/src/style.css` and `web/tailwind.config.js` (if added) to match your brand.
- [ ] **Assets**: Replace or add favicons and static assets in the `web/public` directory or directly in `web/src`.
{{- end}}

{{- if .Features.DB}}
## Database
- [ ] **Configuration**: Update the database credentials in `{{.AppName}}-config.toml` or set the appropriate environment variables.
- [ ] **Schema Migrations**: The project provides a `internal/db/schema.sql` for initial setup. Consider adding a migration tool like `golang-migrate/migrate` or `pressly/goose` for managing schema evolution.
{{- end}}

{{- if .Features.Cache}}
## Cache
- [ ] **Configuration**: Update the cache connection details (host, port, password) in `{{.AppName}}-config.toml`.
{{- end}}

{{- if .Features.Docker}}
## Docker
- [ ] **Registry**: Update the Docker tag registry prefix in `Taskfile.yml` or your CI pipelines before pushing the image.
{{- end}}

{{- if .Features.Nomad}}
## Nomad
- [ ] **Deployment**: Review the `{{.AppName}}.nomad` job file. Adjust CPU/Memory constraints, network ports, and the Docker image name/tag before running `nomad job run`.
{{- end}}

{{- if .Features.Otel}}
## Observability (OpenTelemetry)
- [ ] **OTLP Endpoint**: The OpenTelemetry setup in `internal/otel/otel.go` defaults to `localhost:4317`. Set the `OTEL_EXPORTER_OTLP_ENDPOINT` environment variable in your deployment environment to point to your actual OTLP collector (e.g., Jaeger, Datadog, Honeycomb).
{{- end}}

## General
- [ ] **Dependencies**: Run `go mod tidy` if you add any new imports. (This was run automatically during scaffolding).
- [ ] **Tests**: Run `task test` to ensure all generated components pass their initial unit tests.
